# TypeScript Coding Standards

## Type Safety

- Always use strict TypeScript configuration as defined in [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json)
- Use explicit types for function parameters and return values
- Avoid `any` type - use proper TypeScript interfaces and types
- Use `interface` for object shapes and `type` for unions/intersections

## Performance Patterns

- Implement caching for expensive operations (see [PerformanceOptimizer.ts](mdc:src/PerformanceOptimizer.ts))
- Use Map-based lookups for fast token recognition
- Implement LRU cache management for memory efficiency
- Add performance monitoring and statistics

## Error Handling

- Use proper error interfaces: `ValidationError`, `ParseError`
- Include line and column numbers in error messages
- Provide helpful suggestions in error objects
- Use severity levels: 'error', 'warning', 'info'

## Code Organization

- Export main functions from [src/index.ts](mdc:src/index.ts)
- Keep core logic in dedicated classes (SnowflakeSQL, PerformanceOptimizer)
- Use visitor pattern for custom validation rules
- Separate concerns: parsing, validation, performance optimization

## ANTLR4 Integration

- Generated ANTLR4 files are in [src/parser/snowflake/](mdc:src/parser/snowflake/)
- Don't modify generated files directly - update grammar files instead
- Use visitor pattern for custom validation logic
- Handle parse tree traversal efficiently

## Testing

- Write comprehensive tests in [src/__tests__/](mdc:src/__tests__/)
- Include performance tests for optimization features
- Test case-insensitive keyword handling
- Test caching behavior and memory management
